title: A Brussels Conditionality File
subtitle: EU money, legal commitments and democratic legitimacy arrive in one envelope.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_foreign_card
frequency: 100
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and year >= 2020 and poland_brussels_pressure_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_brussels_pressure_timer = 6; foreign_cards_resolved += 1; foreign_pressure += 2
card-image: img/poland/cards/government-affairs.webp

= A Brussels conditionality file

[? if left_in_government: The cabinet must decide whether a Commission
benchmark is a rule to meet, a political bargain to renegotiate, or an
intrusion to resist. Lewica cannot keep the money and assign every condition
to its coalition partners.?]
[? if not left_in_government: The government owns implementation, but the
opposition still chooses whether to defend common rules, bargain over their
social cost, or join the sovereignty offensive.?]

**Institutional trust:** [+ eu_institutional_trust +]/100 · **external
pressure:** [+ foreign_pressure +]/100.

- @benchmarks
- @social_clause
- @sovereignty

@benchmarks
title: Accept published benchmarks and demand an auditable timetable
subtitle: EU trust +6, restraint +3 and pressure −5; relations with PiS −3.
on-arrival: eu_institutional_trust += 6; eu_influence += 2; constitutional_restraint += 3; government_procedural_restraint += 2 if left_in_government = 1; government_delivery += 2 if left_in_government = 1; pis_relation -= 3; public_trust += 2; foreign_pressure -= 5; news_headline = "The European dispute receives benchmarks, dates and an audit"

The line is legible in Warsaw and Brussels. It may still fail in court or in
the Sejm, but neither side can quietly redefine compliance after the vote.

- #poland_card_finish

@social_clause
title: Negotiate a social-investment safeguard around the conditions
subtitle: Labour credibility +4 and European-left network +5; fiscal stress +2.
on-arrival: eu_left_network += 5; eu_influence += 3; labor_credibility += 4; household_security += 2; fiscal_stress += 2; ko_relation -= 1; foreign_pressure -= 2; news_headline = "The Left makes social capacity part of the European bargain"

The Left accepts common rules while arguing that court repair, climate
transition and migration administration cannot be delivered by hollowed-out
public institutions.

- #poland_card_finish

@sovereignty
title: Reject the file as political coercion
subtitle: PiS relations +4; EU trust −7, far-right agenda +4 and pressure +5.
on-arrival: pis_relation += 4; barons_dissent -= 2; eu_institutional_trust -= 7; eu_influence -= 4; constitutional_restraint -= 2; far_right_agenda += 4; foreign_pressure += 5; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The Left joins a sovereignty front against Brussels"

The government gains room at home and less room in the negotiation. PiS
welcomes the language and asks why voters need a left-wing version of it.

- #poland_card_finish
